:name: MIMXRT1189-EVK — M2 rpmsg_lite_pingpong
:description: Stock NXP SDK demo_apps/hello_world, cm33, --config debug

using sysbus
include @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/scripts/load_peripherals.resc

mach create "rt1180"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/platforms/mimxrt1189_m2.repl


# ⭐ BLANKET TrustZone-M SECURE MIRROR.
# The whole NS peripheral window 0x4000_0000..0x4FFF_FFFF is mirrored at
# 0x5000_0000 in ONE statement, instead of giving each peripheral its own
# "+0x1000_0000" registration.
#
# WHY: per-peripheral aliasing is structurally prone to silently omitting the
# secure alias of any block the test corpus never touches secure-side. That is
# not hypothetical -- it happened here: S3MU was the ONE block without its alias,
# because every NXP SDK example runs non-secure, and only Zephyr (which runs the
# cm33 SECURE) exposed it by polling S3MU TSR at 0x5754_0124.
# A blanket mirror is immune by construction.
# Architecture noted by @rt1180emulator, whose QEMU SoC does the same thing with
# one memory_region_init_alias(0x40000000, size 0x10000000) mapped at 0x50000000.
sysbus Redirect 0x50000000 0x40000000 0x10000000

showAnalyzer lpuart1

cpu PerformanceInMips 240
# ⚠ THIS COMMENT USED TO SAY 798, AND THE ARITHMETIC IN IT WAS WRONG.
# It claimed "798 = the core-clock the M7 firmware passes to SDK_DelayAtLeastUs
# (literal 0x2FAF0800)". But 0x2FAF0800 = 800,000,000, not 798,000,000 -- so the
# constant I derived from it matched NEITHER source. Three numbers are in play:
#   800 MHz  the firmware's delay-loop argument, a conservative MAXIMUM for a
#            busy-wait (SDK_DEVICE_MAXIMUM_CPU_CLOCK_FREQUENCY shape), and NXP's
#            headline figure for the part;
#   792 MHz  the clock the board ACTUALLY configures -- ARM PLL loopDivider 132,
#            postDivider 2 => 24 MHz * 132/(2*2) = 792 MHz (SDK
#            project_template/clock_config.c), and CMSIS
#            system_MIMXRT1189_cm7.h:73 DEFAULT_SYSTEM_CLOCK = 792000000UL;
#   798 MHz  mine, from bad arithmetic on the first of those.
# The configured clock is what a core runs at, so: 792. Same IPC=1 approximation.
cpu1 PerformanceInMips 792


# $elf defaults to the PINNED artifact (MANIFEST.sha256) so this script is
# self-contained and provably runs the same bytes QEMU is given.
$elf?=@/home/kyle/.cache/rt1180-artifacts/sdk/rpmsg_lite_pingpong_primary_core_cm33.elf

macro reset
"""
    # ⚠ THE M7 MUST START HELD. Renode starts every CPU running by default; the
    # RT1180's M7 comes out of reset PARKED (M7_CFG.WAIT resets HIGH) and runs
    # only after the M33 performs the two-gate release. Without this the M7
    # executes the M33's image from the shared bus -- observed directly: eDMA
    # writes tagged "[cpu1: 0xFFE1AB4]", i.e. the M7 running InitCM7DMA.
    cpu1 IsHalted true
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
"""
runMacro $reset
